      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks wrong.\n\n**The problem:** Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is 5 times the usual maximum of 10 mg/day. Typical adult dosing starts at 2.5\u20135 mg once daily and goes up to 10 mg once daily at most. At 50 mg, the patient could get severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia and possibly shock. Amlodipine overdose is also hard to reverse because the drug stays in the body for a long time (half-life of about 30\u201350 hours).\n\n**Possible mix-ups:**\n- Was the intended dose **5 mg** (an extra zero)?\n- Or was a different drug meant? For example, **atenolol 50 mg** or **losartan 50 mg** are common 50 mg antihypertensive doses.\n\nPlease let me know the dose or drug you meant, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 50 mg, tell me the clinical reason. I'd recommend getting pharmacy to review it before it goes in."
      }
