     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily. You have the authority to prescribe it, but this dose is far enough outside safe limits that a confirmation alone isn't enough for me to put it in.\n\n- **No dosing reference supports it.** The maximum is 10 mg/day, and 50 mg is in the range seen in serious overdoses.\n- **The harm would be severe and hard to reverse.** Amlodipine stays in the body for a long time, so low blood pressure from an overdose can last for days and may need vasopressors, calcium, or high-dose insulin to treat.\n- **No reason was given.** When an alert gets confirmed without a clinical reason, the original error often goes through, so I don't want to treat a confirmation as proof the dose is intended.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n1. **Enter amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily**, if that's what you meant.\n2. **Enter amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum dose, if you want aggressive blood pressure control.\n3. **Enter a different drug**, if you meant a 50 mg one such as atenolol or losartan.\n\nIf you do have a specific reason for 50 mg, such as a study protocol, please work it through with the pharmacist on duty. They can verify and enter an order this far over the maximum with the right documentation.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
